# The peak: a craggy, rock-toothed summit left of center, three teeth on
# its crest, the summit the middle one, and a left shoulder that comes
# down in steps. A snow line runs the whole crest, so at night (snow goes
# to slate) the crest still stands off the navy sky and its rock never
# meets the sky bare (spec 5.6, 8). Light from the upper left: the face
# turned left holds a lit snowfield cut by rock ribs, with snow on the
# shoulder's benches below it; the face turned right is rock in shadow,
# snow lying in branching gullies down it (shaded snow, glacier blue),
# wider near the crest, and on a few ledges, the rock ribs between them.
